  "finding": "Stacking more than halves missed frauds (142 -> 69) but does NOT beat the parameter-free rank average (0.4615 vs 0.4791 AUC-PR). The meta-learner is fitted on 2018, where XGBoost looks strong, so it gives XGBoost the larger weight (1.495 vs 0.906). XGBoost then degrades 45% into 2019 while GraphSAGE degrades 11%, so the fitted combiner over-weights the model that ages worse. Under temporal drift, a combiner fitted on a validation period inherits that period's ranking of the base models.",
  "recommendation": "Use the unfitted rank average: best AUC-PR (0.4791), fewest missed frauds (59 vs 142 for GraphSAGE alone) at the same alert budget, and no fitted parameter that can go stale.",
  "caveat": "Both base models early-stopped on 2018, so it is a validation set rather than a clean out-of-fold set. Proper out-of-fold base predictions would need k-fold retraining of the GNN."
